From 9d57ad059d60b4a7baa3afba3d3c2d3502d6f36a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: teleop-bench <325283884+teleop-bench@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 00:14:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] M0 FSU: defect fixes + HCI bridge on top of PR#99473
 reference

Fixes per zephyr-patches/fsu-m0-cheatsheet.md defect list: inverted
change-detection comparisons; tifs_hcto_us follows tifs_rx_us; wrong
CONFIG_BT_PHY_UPDATE guard -> CONFIG_BT_CTLR_PHY; debug printk removed;
range validation (min<=max, <=10ms) in ull_cp_fsu; eff.phys/spacing_type
preserved for the ntf encoder before request-scratch clearing.

New: Kconfig.ll_sw_split selects FRAME_SPACE_UPDATE_SUPPORT +
EXTENDED_FEAT_SET_SUPPORT; BT_CTLR_FSU_BENCH_FORCE_FEAT bench shim
(documented non-conformant: forces feature_fsu known-supported; bit 65
exceeds the 64-bit LLCP mask; UNKNOWN_RSP path handles non-support).
HCI bridge: LE Frame Space Update cmd 0x209D -> bt_ull_cp_fsu (cmd
status); LE Read All Local Supported Features 0x2087 (max_page=1, bit 65
= byte8 bit1) + supported-commands octet 47 bit 2 so the host's
extended-feature read path lights up; FSU Complete meta event 0x35 from
the FSU_RSP ntf (initiator by role per M0 single-initiator convention).

NOT upstreamable as-is (bench shim; no real feature-page exchange - M1).
