From 6a2245e1dc81d3cfd5b21d1443dda1656e1e7371 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: teleop-bench <325283884+teleop-bench@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 00:36:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] M0 FSU WORKING: transitional receive windows +
 RSP-from-effective-state

Two on-air-discovered fixes. (1) Transitional windows (the spec's model,
absent from the reference): the responder adopts before its RSP, so the
RSP flies at the NEW spacing while the initiator still listens with old
timing - without bridging, both ends deadlock at different spacings and
the link dies 0x08 within seconds (observed 5x/60s). Fix: RX-enable
adopts the reduced spacing early (initiator at REQ enqueue, both roles at
adoption) while tifs_hcto stays at the old/default spacing, so both
timings are heard. Result: 0 disconnects across all subsequent runs.
(2) The reference clears the request-scratch masks after adoption, and
encode_fsu_rsp read those cleared fields -> RSP carried phys=0/types=0,
the initiator matched no branch, committed nothing, reported nothing.
Fix: mirror masks into fsu.eff unconditionally before clearing; RSP and
ntf encode from eff; eff masks initialized.

Verified on two nRF54L15-DK: FSU Complete on the host callback,
status=0x00 spacing=52us phys=0x3 types=0x3, disc=0 - negotiated 52us on
the fully open stack (below the SDC's 70us floor).
